claim.claim-text:
causing a plurality of microdroplets to travel out of a dosing head of a dosing system toward the food product, the microdroplets containing the active pharmaceutical ingredient that includes a cannabinoid;
measuring a cross-sectional dimension of each of the microdroplets with a camera as the microdroplets travel from the dosing head to the food product; and
based on the measuring step, calculating an approximation of a volume of the microdroplets delivered to the food product.

a dosing head configured to deliver a plurality of microdroplets to the food product, wherein the microdroplets contain the active pharmaceutical ingredient that includes a cannabinoid;
a camera configured to measure a cross-sectional dimension of each of the microdroplets as the microdroplets travel from the dosing head to the food product,
wherein, the system is configured to calculate an approximation of a volume of the microdroplets delivered to the food product based on the measuring step measured cross-sectional dimension of each of the microdroplets.
